            {
                "entry_id": "e7d9d8b5-5490-32c0-975e-290a165d15b1",
                "word": "overtop",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "7a2d6431-96fc-4034-b777-f71b35eefedf",
                        "entry_id": "e7d9d8b5-5490-32c0-975e-290a165d15b1",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "overtops"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "66516ecd-d72d-3bfb-b557-695a06f3dcda",
                        "entry_id": "e7d9d8b5-5490-32c0-975e-290a165d15b1",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A garment designed to be worn over the top portion of other clothes, such as an overshirt, vest, or overtunic."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "e19a9c5c-0dae-40a0-a05a-bf6fcb8c7317",
                                "sense_id": "66516ecd-d72d-3bfb-b557-695a06f3dcda",
                                "text": "Featured is the big plaid, streaked with white in a softly gathered skirt & an overtop of velveteen with a dacron polytester^([sic]) oliver bow blouse in white."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "6ef128ac-7f5c-45f8-b653-ac5209a531d5",
                                "sense_id": "66516ecd-d72d-3bfb-b557-695a06f3dcda",
                                "text": "A very obvious point, but one easily overlooked, is that children from 0–5 grow all the time, so a garment often only fits perfectly for a short time. So if, for instance, a long sleeved dress worn during the summer is visualized as being worn under an overtop in winter, you will have to allow for 6 months’ growth."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "fb640a1b-c5a2-4b85-9d4a-cf226995b7f5",
                                "sense_id": "66516ecd-d72d-3bfb-b557-695a06f3dcda",
                                "text": "Brown soft kid belt (dressier day): for trousers (especially when you belt an overtop), skirts, dresses."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "ee6491c7-078d-4a16-849d-8d948c4e0d97",
                                "sense_id": "66516ecd-d72d-3bfb-b557-695a06f3dcda",
                                "text": "And I bought that top in every colour they had, and if they’d had more I would have bought them too. I have, literally, lived in them all this summer and know that I will all next summer too. I may even wear the darker coloured ones in the winter with a turtle-neck sweater underneath. Janis and Ozzie are wearing them on p. 150. As you can see, you can either wear this as a dress or as an overtop."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "4297c101-0a0f-47d6-b174-6f84ed3600b4",
                                "sense_id": "66516ecd-d72d-3bfb-b557-695a06f3dcda",
                                "text": "The use of the second contrast yarn (which is thick and braid like) gives the appearance of a ribbon threaded through. Not only is this a satisfying pattern to work but the sweater can be worn for day or evening; with skirt or trousers: as a sweater or an overtop—a sufficiently versatile garment for anyone."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "3800415d-ef8d-4258-a32b-adce33b8fa36",
                                "sense_id": "66516ecd-d72d-3bfb-b557-695a06f3dcda",
                                "text": "Skirts can also be fitted with a hip yoke to replace darts or gores. This is effective styling for a skirt worn with an overtop."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [],
                "word_linkages": []
            },
            {
