                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "53f94d91-8f7b-3379-a368-14e883afddb0",
                        "entry_id": "19ed6be7-e106-3755-bdac-d34a65c23b38",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To be higher than; to rise over the top of."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "transitive"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "5ceb2e9b-9d19-492b-9554-3a44e3c4aae9",
                                "sense_id": "53f94d91-8f7b-3379-a368-14e883afddb0",
                                "text": "From thence we came without the Eaſtern gate, (ſtanding on a low Banke, called the daughter of Syon, that over-toppeth the valley of Iehoſaphat,) unto an immoveable ſtone, upon the which they ſaid St. Stephen was ſtoned to death, the firſt Martyr of the Chriſtian faith; and the faithfull fore-runner of many noble followers."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "d397973e-49c5-40e7-9b7c-1dc9bb9bea04",
                                "sense_id": "53f94d91-8f7b-3379-a368-14e883afddb0",
                                "text": "Nor was he content with thus strongly garrisoning the fort, but he likewise added exceedingly to its strength by furnishing it with a formidable battery of quaker guns—rearing a stupendous flag-staff in the centre which overtopped the whole city—and moreover by building a great windmill on one of the bastions."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "5b31baa8-d328-409e-90b4-40adba374247",
                                "sense_id": "53f94d91-8f7b-3379-a368-14e883afddb0",
                                "text": "There was a single birch tree that overtopped the other trees on the island, and was now picked out against the moon-drenched sky."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "a6e126bd-fcdb-4ef4-a7e6-250d61b53d80",
                                "sense_id": "53f94d91-8f7b-3379-a368-14e883afddb0",
                                "text": "The U.S.A. has a mountain railway which overtops all in Switzerland for altitude, even the 11,333ft of the Jungfrau Railway."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "68e8200e-41f9-413c-bbd8-b239898172b1",
                                "sense_id": "53f94d91-8f7b-3379-a368-14e883afddb0",
                                "text": "[…] try to switch one off and current still leaks through, like water overtopping a levee."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "e7ab25e0-21d8-32da-a38d-9debeb5844a4",
                        "entry_id": "19ed6be7-e106-3755-bdac-d34a65c23b38",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To place too many toppings on."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "transitive"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "659878a1-bf37-4ee4-9444-d81b608317d5",
                                "sense_id": "e7ab25e0-21d8-32da-a38d-9debeb5844a4",
                                "text": "to overtop a pizza"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
